# Gherkin `.feature` files are declarative specs reviewed like prose (ADR 020).
# Diff them with git's built-in markdown hunk-header driver so review diffs read
# as behaviour changes rather than code, and normalise line endings.
*.feature diff=markdown
*.feature text eol=lf

# Docs-corpus machine-owned manifest (FE-2752, design §8.1/§8.2). These paths are
# derived build artifacts, never hand-authored (ADR-026 decision 1). `linguist-
# generated=true` collapses their MR diff noise; `eol=lf` pins line endings so the
# authorship guard's byte-exact regen-and-compare (gate:authorship, §8.2 check 1)
# is environment-independent — a CRLF checkout can never false-RED against the
# LF CI re-emit.
docs/published-docs/developers/reference/**       linguist-generated=true text eol=lf
docs/published-docs/developers/changelog/**       linguist-generated=true text eol=lf
docs/published-docs/developers/corpus-version.json linguist-generated=true text eol=lf
docs/corpus/corpus.json          linguist-generated=true text eol=lf
docs/corpus/relations.json       linguist-generated=true text eol=lf
